    {
      "path": ".claude/scripts/full-suite.sh",
      "content": "With Git's default rename detection, --name-only lists only the destination of a rename. Moving a file out of src/ui/ (or another full-tier directory) into an unlisted directory can therefore return `task`, even though the change removes a protected source path. Use --no-renames so both paths are checked, or inspect both sides of renames via --name-status.",
      "suggestion_code": "  paths=$(git diff --no-renames --name-only \"$1\" HEAD) || return 2",
      "existing_code": "  paths=$(git diff --name-only \"$1\" HEAD) || return 2",
      "start_line": 47,
      "end_line": 47,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": ".claude/scripts/full-suite.sh",
      "content": "Git quotes paths containing non-ASCII characters (with the default `core.quotePath=true`), as well as tabs or quotes. For example, a change only to `src/ui/é.tsx` is returned as a quoted, escaped path, so it matches none of these patterns and incorrectly selects the task tier. Read NUL-delimited paths with `git diff --name-only -z` and `read -r -d ''` (without storing the NUL-delimited output in a shell variable) so the rule operates on literal filenames.",
